<p style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt; text-align: right;">EXECUTIVE COMPENSATION</p>

<p style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt; text-align: right;">&#160;</p>

<hr style="height: 1px; color: #000000; background-color: #000000; width: 100%; border: none; margin: 3pt 0"/>
<p style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt; text-align: left">&#160;</p>

<table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%; text-indent: 0px;">

		<tbody><tr style="vertical-align: top;">
			<td style="width: 18pt;">
			<p style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif;font-size: 10pt;font-variant:normal;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;">(7)</p>
			</td>
			<td style="width: auto;">
			<p style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif;font-size: 10pt;font-variant:normal;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;">For fiscal years 2025, 2024 and 2023, calculation of our PEO&#8217;s CAP reflects adjustments made to the total compensation amounts reported in the Summary Compensation Table (&#8220;SCT&#8221;) for those fiscal year, computed in accordance with Item 402(v) of Regulation&#160;S-K. The CAP dollar amounts included in the table do not reflect the actual amount of compensation earned by the executive or paid by us during the applicable year.&#160;The adjustments made to the SCT total for purposes of calculating CAP, in accordance with the relevant rules, are reflected below:</p>
			</td>
		</tr>

</tbody></table>
</ix:nonNumeric>

<p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>

